.TH CARBON\-REGION\-PICKER 1 "2026-09" "carbon-region-picker" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
carbon-region-picker \- rank cloud regions by grid carbon intensity, under a latency constraint
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B carbon-region-picker
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Ranks a cloud provider's regions by the carbon intensity of their
electricity grid, subject to a latency budget from a chosen vantage point \(em
so the answer is a region you can actually deploy to, not merely a clean one.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-provider " NAME"
Cloud provider (default aws).
.TP
.BI \-\-near " VANTAGE"
Latency vantage point (default eu).
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-latency\-ms " MS"
Reject regions slower than this.
.TP
.B \-\-measure
Probe real TCP latency to each region's endpoint instead of using the
bundled estimate. AWS and GCP only.
.TP
.B \-\-live
Use Electricity Maps real-time data instead of bundled averages.
.TP
.B \-\-marginal
Use marginal rather than average grid intensity. Requires
.BR \-\-live .
.TP
.B \-\-forecast
Suggest the cleanest hour in the next 24 for the top region. Requires
.BR \-\-live .
.TP
.BI \-\-em\-token " TOKEN"
Electricity Maps API token. Prefer the
.I EM_TOKEN
environment variable: a token passed here is visible in the process list.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable output.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
A ranking was produced.
.TP
.B non-zero
No region met the constraints, or the data source failed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Cleanest European region within 60 ms:
.PP
.RS
.B carbon-region-picker \-\-provider aws \-\-near eu \-\-max\-latency\-ms 60
.RE
.PP
Against live grid data:
.PP
.RS
.B carbon-region-picker \-\-provider aws \-\-live
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR carbon-badge (1).
Project documentation:
https://github.com/fabiocicerchia/carbon-region-picker
